# Citation metadata for this repository.
#
# Deliberately sparse. Every field below is something we can point at in the
# repository itself. There is no DOI, no ORCID and no institutional
# affiliation here, because the project has none of those and inventing them in
# a machine-readable file is how a fabricated citation ends up in somebody
# else's bibliography.
#
# Author names are exactly the names published in README.md. Three of the four
# are given names only; that is how the team writes them, and guessing family
# names would be worse than omitting them. If you are one of the four, add your
# own family name and, if you have one, your ORCID, in a pull request.
#
# Format: Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this project, please cite it using the metadata in this file,
  and please carry the prototype notice with it: the platform holds no real
  KuwaitSat-1 data and every figure in it is invented for demonstration.
title: "KuwaitSat Green Intelligence — KuwaitSat-1 Mission Hub"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A student capstone prototype of a secure, bilingual (English and Arabic,
  full right-to-left) research console for Earth-observation work over Kuwait.
  A signed-in researcher states an environmental objective, an area and a
  period; a pipeline of agents proposes findings, and a human gate stands
  before monitoring and before the written study. Per-researcher isolation is
  enforced by PostgreSQL row-level security rather than by the page. The
  platform is not affiliated with the KuwaitSat-1 project, Kuwait University,
  KFAS, CITRA or SACGC, holds no real satellite imagery or telemetry, and is
  not an official government planning system.
authors:
  - given-names: Retag
  - given-names: Hind
  - given-names: Mariam
    family-names: Madouh
    alias: t021600-dot
  - given-names: Dana
repository-code: "https://github.com/t021600-dot/KuwaitSat1Hub"
url: "https://kuwait-sat1-hub.vercel.app/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - kuwaitsat-1
  - earth-observation
  - row-level-security
  - human-in-the-loop
  - prompt-injection
  - bilingual
  - right-to-left
  - supabase
  - capstone
  - prototype
